## 1. Executive Summary &amp; Aesthetic Architecture

The **Cybernetic Rāga Durgā &amp; 22-Shruti Microtonal Music Studio** is an interactive, browser-playable microtonal acoustics laboratory implemented directly within the UOS knowledge mesh. It unites ancient Indian classical musicology (*Gandharva Veda*, Bharata&#39;s *Natya Shastra*, and Sarangadeva&#39;s *Sangita Ratnakara*) with contemporary complex systems cybernetics (Luis M. Rocha&#39;s biosemiotics, Gordon Pask&#39;s conversation theory, and W. Ross Ashby&#39;s law of requisite variety).

Operating under strict Zero-Muda and OTP 29 supervision, this studio enables operators, researchers, and autonomous agent swarms to synthesize, explore, and audition pure just intonation intervals, acoustic bamboo flute (*Bānsurī*) timbres with natural *Meend* (continuous portamento glide), organic four-string *Tanpura* harmonic drone cascades with non-linear *Jawari* buzzing, and authentic 16-beat *Teentaal* rhythms on the *Tabla* (featuring modulated pitch-sliding *Bayan* strokes).

